Spec: Caller-bound Android business runtime

Purpose:
  Connect approved local scopes through authenticated peers and attach one-use Binder descriptors.

Owns:
  ./AgentConnections.java

References:
  /agent-core/src/main/java/dev/linkgate/agent/AgentRegistry.sdd
  /transport-core/src/main/java/dev/linkgate/transport/PeerClient.sdd
  /android/descriptor-core/descriptor-core.sdd

Must:
  Journal opens before dialing and cap active runtime streams at `16` per caller and `32` globally.
  Capture the caller before attachment, reject stolen or repeated operations and require descriptor acknowledgement within ten seconds.
  Abort transports and descriptors before asynchronous persistence so storage delay cannot extend revoked business access.
  Preserve half-close and backpressure, close on caller death or lost authority and never replay payload.
  Keep startup, copy, control, timers and persistence queues separately bounded and stop late opens after shutdown.

  Acquire current server leases for configured server mode on both direct and relay business paths; failed server authorization must not downgrade to preview.
  Hold each relay lease until its corresponding stream closes, release it before deferred journal writes and preserve unrelated flows sharing the same runtime.

  Preserve authenticated server denial and lease verification failure as authorization outcomes; do not report them as an offline transport failure.

  Start the total budget at admission before journal IO, carry it through authorization and route setup, and hand off exactly one planner result.
  A direct-only open may try a bounded known-IPv4 candidate then authenticated XTCP with fallback disabled; explicit relay remains a separate selection.
  Close registered raw abort handles before deferred persistence, including attempts that have not yet become ready.
  Count only selected authenticated direct candidates by LAN or XTCP for owner-side aggregate acceptance; a listening visitor alone is not a successful direct connection.
  Compose the formal connection runtime under the same owner lifetime and bounded workers, recovering its journal only after exclusive startup publication is authorized.
  Reject new attempts during network invalidation, abort old generation IO before recycling owned runtime caches and resume only after invalidation finishes.
